---
title: Apple Cider Donuts
source: https://smittenkitchen.com/2009/10/apple-cider-donuts/
servings: 18
---

== Donuts ==

In a #saucepan{} over medium or medium-low heat, gently reduce @apple cider{1%cup} to about 1/4 cup, ~{20-30%minutes}. Set aside to cool. 

Meanwhile, in a #bowl, combine @flour{3 1/2%cups}, @baking powder{2%teaspoons}, @baking soda{1%teaspoon}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%teaspoon}, @salt{1/2%teaspoon}, and @ground nutmeg{1/8%teaspoon}. Set aside. 

Using a #standing mixer{} on medium speed with the paddle attachment, beat @butter{4%tablespoons}(at room temperature) and @granulated sugar{1%cup} until the mixture is smooth. Add @eggs{2%large}, one at a time, and continue to beat until the eggs are completely incorporated. Use a spatula to scrape down the sides of the bowl occasionally. 

Reduce the speed to low and gradually add the reduced apple cider and @buttermilk{1/2%cup}, mixing just until combined. Add the flour mixture and continue to mix just until the dough comes together. 

Line two #baking sheets{} with parchment or wax paper and sprinkle them generously with flour. Turn the dough onto one of the sheets and sprinkle the top with flour. Flatten the dough with your hands until it is about 1/2 inch thick. Use more flour if the dough is still wet. Transfer the dough to the freezer until it is slightly hardened, about ~{20%minutes}. 

Pull the dough out of the freezer. Using a #donut cutter{} (3-inch or 3.5-inch), cut out donut shapes. Place the cut donuts and donut holes onto the second sheet pan. Refrigerate the donuts for ~{20-30%minutes}. 

Add @vegetable oil or shortening{} to your #deep fryer{} and heat the oil to 350°F.

Carefully add a few donuts to the oil, being careful not to crowd the pan, and fry until golden brown, about ~{60%seconds}. Turn the donuts over and fry until the other side is golden, ~{30%seconds} to ~{60%seconds}. Drain on paper towels for a minute after the donuts are fried.

== Toppings ==

Whisk together @confectioners' sugar{1%cup} and @apple cider{2%tablespoons} until smooth. Make cinnamon sugar by mixing @granulated sugar{1%cup} and @ground cinnamon{1.5%tablespoons} together. Set aside. 

Dip the top of the warm donuts into the glaze or cinnamon sugar mixture (if using) and serve immediately.